Z||000002||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||04-24-2001||06:08 AM||||Supercharged Buick V6 will be very impressive in a Fiero.  <P>The Buick V6 is a legendary engine. (yes, so is a small block Chevy) You get big torquey balls and great MPG in a very reliable engine.  Like the V8, it's not as light as the stock Fiero V6.  But it has almost twice the horsepower and torue.  <P>You already own one.  So, I say a you would be wasting your money to by anything else.  Build it and you will love it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||kitcar||04-24-2001||07:50 AM||||I would of thought the zz4 would make a BIG diff from the 3.8SC...I mean the 3.8SC has only 240HP, the zz4 has 330HP, and way more tourq.  I planned on tacking on a supercharger on the zz4 if i did buy it.  The reason what makes me lean more to the v8, is that i can make it go faster.  By just adding the SC on the zz4 i will be hitting in low 11's i belive.  I have a 2000 trans am right now running on pure motor and im hitting 12.7 right now with only headers.  Just think if my car weighs as much as my fiero does.  Thats 1k pounds lighter!!  That would almost be in the 10's.<P>Thanks for the help you guys.  If you have anymore input please let me know!<P>Archie if you read this, the v8 kit is 950$ right?||||reg||1
